{{head|en|adjective|head=[[back]]-of-the-[[envelope]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[approximate|Approximate]], [[rough]], [[simplified]], especially of a [[calculation]], [[estimation]] or other [[reasoning]].
#: {{ux|en|Do some '''back-of-the-envelope''' calculations before all the facts come in.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=David G. Thomson|title=Mastering the 7 Essentials of High-Growth Companies|date=2010-04-30|publisher=John Wiley & Sons|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=Mq6qABNv_IIC&pg=PT63&dq=%22back-of-the-envelope%22&hl=&cd=33&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22back-of-the-envelope%22&f=false|isbn=978-0-470-63482-0|passage=I remember very distinctly in October 1995, after I completed my paper design, I had an epiphany. This '''back-of-the-envelope''' design was five years ahead of its time.}}

